<h2>What you get</h2>
<p>After OAuth, the agent can search public short-form video, save boards, analyze media, and run deep research on your ContHunt account. Tool groups:</p>
<div class="docs-table-wrap">
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Group</th>
            <th>Tools</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>Search</td><td><code>search_*</code>, <code>agent_search_*</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Creators</td><td><code>creator_get</code>, <code>creator_videos</code>, <code>video_get</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Boards</td><td><code>board_*</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Analysis</td><td><code>analyze_*</code>, <code>insights_*</code>, <code>download_url</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Research</td><td><code>research_*</code> including <code>research_messages</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trending</td><td><code>trending_youtube</code>, <code>trending_tiktok</code>, <code>trending_niches</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Files</td><td><code>workspace_*</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h2>Auth</h2>
<p>The server challenges unauthenticated clients and sends them through ContHunt login. Approve access in the browser. Do not paste API keys into MCP config.</p>
<p>If a client still has an old <code>https://agent.conthunt.app/mcp</code> URL, remove it and add <code>https://mcp.conthunt.app</code>.</p>

<h2>Skill</h2>
<p>Want the agent to know when to use these tools? Install the <a href="/docs/integrations/skill">ContHunt skill</a> from the same domain.</p>

<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>ContHunt uses your account to run research you request. See <a href="/privacy">privacy</a> and <a href="/terms">terms</a>. Support: <a href="mailto:support@conthunt.app">support@conthunt.app</a>.</p>
